<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rato--no &quot;creative accounting&quot; in budget.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rato--no &quot;creative accounting&quot; in budget.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato said on Friday the government had not used creating accounting to assure its 1997 budget draft meets the criteria for Spain's entry into a single European currency.</p>
<p>Speaking shortly after the cabinet approved the draft, Rato said there was no &quot;creative accounting&quot; in the budget.</p>
</text>
